      "_baseline_note_entry": "AUTHORISED RE-RECORD \u2014 this WHOLE ENTRY IS NEW (vyomquant-ui-redesign task 12.3's follow-up, BC-3). ONE ADDITION to `collaborator_sequence`; nothing else in this file moved. WHY THE WRITE EXISTS: BC-3 added `last_signal_at` to the `GET /api/strategies` list projection, but no migration declared the column and nothing on any path wrote it, so the field reported `null` on every database, permanently \u2014 exactly the condition task 12's preamble rules out (\"no field's not-available state is its permanent outcome\"). A projection that can only ever answer `null` is not a field, it is a promise the backend cannot keep. THE PRODUCER THAT CLOSED IT: `backend_app/migrations/015_strategy_last_signal_at.sql` declares the column, and `backend_app/backend/strategy_last_signal.py::record_last_signal_at` performs the `strategies.update` recorded here. It is called from `signal_service._persist_signal` and from `SignalService.create_signal`, in both cases only AFTER the signal row is confirmed persisted \u2014 which is why it sits HERE, immediately after the `signals` insert and before the genesis-row anchor, rather than anywhere earlier. WHY AN ADDED WRITE ON THIS PATH IS ACCEPTABLE AT ALL \u2014 IT IS ISOLATED FROM THE SIGNAL PATH IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: the update is scheduled with `asyncio.create_task` and is NEVER AWAITED by the signal path, so it can neither raise into it nor delay it, and `record_last_signal_at` additionally catches `BaseException` and returns a bool rather than propagating anything to its caller. That isolation is the whole authorisation: the live recording proceeds exactly as captured whether this write succeeds, fails, or never runs at all. THE REST OF THE CAPTURE IS THE EVIDENCE: it lands on a DIFFERENT table (`strategies`, not `signals` and not `order_lifecycle_transitions`), so the lifecycle recording either side of it is untouched \u2014 `genesis_row_was_written` is still true, the `order_lifecycle_transitions` select and insert still follow in that order, and `event_sequence`, `event_row`, `signals_row` and `mode_value` are all as captured. SCOPE: this note covers this one sequence entry. Any other addition to a recorded collaborator sequence, in this file or another, is a failure in its own right, whether or not this note sits nearby.",
